From: devvm <https://github.com/bindreams/devvm>
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386/whpx: do not grant the guest the hypercall registers

QEMU sets AccessHypercallRegs (Bank0 bit 7) in the partition's synthetic
processor features. With it, Hyper-V running inside a Windows guest gets a
broken hypercall page: an inner Linux guest panics in hv_send_ipi and inner WHP
clients die at int3. Microsoft's own VM stack does not break. With only that bit cleared
(Bank0 0x6448fff to 0x6448f7f), inner VMs boot 27 of 27 times, and the guest
measures as fast as before (boot to SSH, SHA256, GZip, 1000 x Sleep(1)).

devvm-specific; applies after 0003.
---
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -3314,7 +3314,7 @@
     synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessVpRunTimeReg = 1;
     synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessPartitionReferenceCounter = 1;
     synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessPartitionReferenceTsc = 1;
-    synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessHypercallRegs = 1;
+    /* AccessHypercallRegs stays clear: with it, a guest's Hyper-V breaks. */
     synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessFrequencyRegs = 1;
     synthetic_features.Bank0.AccessVpIndex = 1;
 
